From 10d5f55f205c3359549036264095af140540ee0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "huimin.he" <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:55:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: add MT7987 WED support from MediaTek SDK

On MT7987 the WED attach fails ("failed to attach wed device"):
upstream mtk_wed treats every NETSYS v3 SoC as MT7988 and requires the
WO MCU (wo-dlm/wo-emi/wo-data reserved memory, WO firmware), which
MT7987 does not have.

Port the WED support from mtk-openwrt-feeds (25.12, fb7d0538):

kernel (target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12):
- 999-wed-01..05, 08..10, 14..18, 20..22: add the MT7987 WED v3.1
  hardware path (no WO, RRO 3.1) and related WED fixes.
- wed-07/11/13/19 are left out, they depend on SDK PPE/ethernet
  patches that are not in this tree and are not needed by mt76.

mt76 (package/kernel/mt76/patches):
- WED related SDK patches 0023, 0040, 0041, 0047, 0048, 0049, 0090,
  rebased onto mt76 39c960c3.
- adapt mt7915/mt7996 to wlan.wpdma_tx becoming an array.
- separate host and WED tx token ranges: with the MT7987 hw path WED
  owns tokens [0, 16384), so move the host pool after it as the SDK
  does (part of its 0054 debug-tools patch). Otherwise WED stalls on
  the txfree ring, ALTX/beacons stop and the SSID disappears shortly
  after boot.

Signed-off-by: huimin.he <huimin.he@cybertan.com.tw>
